  default serves other bench call sites too; changing it is a separate call)
- `tests/test_golden_fixture_harness.py` — proves the machinery on invented
  one-item data; does not exercise the real multi-document/multi-language
  shape (see "What is proven" above)
- `SPEC.md:1008`, `SPEC.md:2455` — the two extraction-cap citations this
  ticket traced and pinned

## Exit criteria
- [x] the existing injection-script/export-snapshot/Zotero-free-replay
      mechanism is read and verified generically correct against the real
      17-document, multi-language, multi-archive recipe shape (by code
      inspection; no live run possible without the group below) —
      **narrower than it reads**: this proved genericity over document
      count/language/format, never compatibility with a live group
      library, and those turned out to be different axes (see the
      2026-09-04 log entry: the real run failed on a hardcoded
      `linkMode: "linked_file"` group libraries categorically refuse,
      which no code-reading pass caught and no invented test could have,
      since the mocked client enforces none of Zotero's real business
      rules)
- [x] the `index_fulltext_max_chars` discrepancy flagged in 0029's log
      (2026-09-02 22:41Z scoping brief) is pinned with a stated reason
      (40000, matching the shipped `DEFAULT_FULLTEXT_MAX_CHARS`)
- [x] the exact injection/export commands are staged, with every required
      input identified and its source stated (client version and both
      extraction preferences read from the live client at run time, per the
      tool's own no-silent-defaults design) — staged correctly; running
      them surfaced the linked-file defect below, which is a defect in
      what the commands ask Zotero to do, not in the staging
- [x] the group and local-API blockers are cleared (author, 2026-09-04) and
      independently re-verified: group 6659303 PublicClosed, collection
      3AY48MA5, `ZOTEUS_LOCAL_API_KEY` granted, `bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin`
      installed and responding
- [ ] a real injection into the dedicated public Zotero group, and a real
      export snapshot committed under `bench/fixtures/`, replayed through
      the offline harness and `bench/golden_gate.py` end-to-end — **blocked
      on a new finding, not the group**: Zotero refuses linked-file
      attachments in any group library (DECISIONS.md, 2026-09-04 finding).
      Needs an author decision on how to hold the bytes (stored attachment
      against the group owner's storage quota, WebDAV, a reduced interim
      footprint, or another approach) before this can proceed
- [ ] ticket 0029's own "injection script"/"export snapshot committed"/
      "Zotero-free index-build harness" exit-criteria bullets ticked, once
      the above is real
